(
 '* 3.1.3 from 2026-11-25'
 '  * `SendEmailExample` changed: the shared Gmail account it used no longer exists, so it now takes an'
 '    instance of `ConnectionParameters` with your own credentials as left argument. Attachments, the left'
 '    argument so far, are now passed after the email address on the right. When sending failed, its result'
 '    lacked the error message; fixed.'
 '  * Bug fixes:'
 '    * The body was not dot-stuffed: a line consisting of a single dot ended the message early, and the'
 '      lines after it were sent to the server as SMTP commands.'
 '    * Sending failed with an INDEX ERROR on Windows machines without daylight saving time, and time zones'
 '      with half hours got a wrong offset. The "Date" header is now built with ⎕DT, the same on all platforms.'
 '    * AUTH PLAIN failed with a SYNTAX ERROR.'
 '    * The "X-Mailer" header read "APLTeam SMTP Client ." instead of carrying the version number.'
 '    * An address without a dot in the domain, like kai@localhost, caused a DOMAIN ERROR. Addresses that'
 '      cannot be used are now reported through the result of `Send`.'
 '    * Display names, "Organization" and "Reply-To" with characters above ⎕UCS 127 were encoded wrongly.'
 '    * Addresses (`To`, `CC`, `BCC`, `From`, `ReplyTo`) and `Org` refused characters above ⎕UCS 255, and'
 '      `Subject` and `Body` refused characters above ⎕UCS 65535, emojis for example. All accept any Unicode'
 '      character now; only the email address itself must be ASCII, as SMTPUTF8 is not supported.'
 '    * A password with characters above ⎕UCS 255 was refused; it is now sent as UTF-8.'
 '    * The closing MIME boundary was missing.'
 '    * An attachment whose file had disappeared caused a RANK ERROR instead of an error message.'
 '    * Long header lines were not folded, and an empty "CC:" header was sent for an email without CC.'
 '    * `ConnectionParameters.Domain` did not follow changes of `Userid` once it had been read.'
 '    * Once the server had closed the connection, which servers do after a few minutes of inactivity,'
 '      every further `Send` through the same `Connection` failed. `Send` now connects and logs on again.'
 '    * A relay that does not ask for authentication could not be used: without a password, `SMTP` now'
 '      does not authenticate at all.'
 '    * A server offering neither AUTH LOGIN nor AUTH PLAIN caused a DOMAIN ERROR instead of an error'
 '      message in the result of `Send`.'
 '    * A response to EHLO in more than one part lost the line break between the parts, so an AUTH line'
 '      in the second part could be missed; and a response in more than two parts was not read completely.'
 '    * `Connection.CongaRef` set to the name of the Conga namespace did not work.'
 '  * Removed: `Connection.Xmit`, `Connection.Conx` and `Message.Send`. None of them was documented,'
 '    `Conx` was always empty, and `Message.Send` could not work.'
 '  * Security: CR and LF are refused in all properties that end up in a header line or an SMTP command.'
 '  * The test cases no longer need a mail account or a human confirming receipt: they talk to a fake SMTP'
 '    server running in the workspace. An optional live test reads its credentials from a file named in'
 '    the environment variable SMTP_TEST_CONFIG.'
 '  * Documentation corrected and completed, `SendEmailExample` documentation added to `Help`.'
 '* 3.1.2 from 2026-08-25'
 '  * When more than one CC: was specified, some servers rejected because more than one "RCPT TO:" was specified'
 '  * `Connection.Send` printed a 0 to the session when an error occurred.'
 '  * The return codes for specifying CCs was not checked'
 '* 3.1.1 from 2025-09-16'
 '  * Bug fix in the constructor of `ConnectionParameters`'
 '* 3.1.0 from 2025-09-10'
 '  * LICENSE updated'
 '  * Bug fix: when `Version` was called an empty vector was returned.'
 '* 3.0.1 from 2025-06-29'
 '  * HTML emails were not recognized as such'
 '* 3.0.0 from 2025-04-09'
 '  * Potentially breaking: `Version` now returns a simple character vector stemming from the package config file'
 '  * "Make" improved'
 '  * Packages updated'
 '* 2.1.0 from 2022-09-10'
 '  * Documentation needed an update because Google has replaced the "Allow access from unsafe apps" by a more'
 '    secure mechanism. The software however remained unchanged.'
 '* 2.0.1 from 2022-08-03'
 '  * Test cases amended according to the changes Google introduced for unsafe applications'
 '  * New "Make": uses the MakeHelpers package, which is expected to be available in ⎕SE.'
 '* 2.0.0 from 2021-12-21'
 '  * First version'
)
